{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/live_build.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:00:54.225097Z","id":"8a22fe8fcacdab6159022cceee1a56f4613564d28fb8b4ca8568683e1b133600","body":{"detail":"Only flutter analyze and the scripted smoke test (apps/clax_app/test/eval/eval_harness_test.dart) cover this file. Unverified until the first keyed run: that `flutter run -d macos -t tool/eval/live_build.dart` (tool/eval/run.sh) passes the parent environment through to the app (flutter_tools desktop_device.dart starts the executable with the parent's environment), that exit() ends `flutter run`, and that the daemon from tool/test-bin.sh serves the shell for the WebViews. The first run with a key should use one cheap prompt: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=… just app-eval --prompts workouts --model claude-haiku-5-5 --max-spend 6`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":187},"content_hash":"67d3ba76db05031684ffbee322bbcc7f66b52bd7c0246134e916bfcb52e15c36"},"summary":"The live eval app has never run: no API key on the machine, and building it would share apps/clax_app/build/macos with the integration tests","tags":["unverified","revisit:the first eval run with an API key","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/live_build.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:00:54.225199Z","id":"11c42dd2b34d33057e097fba1b1dfa170676deb416f2f89bb3df5ba557f39a23","body":{"detail":"_Host places each inspector's surface at its size with Clip.none; the screenshot is drawn by the page (web/shell/src/app/host.ts `inspection`), so the WebView's frame width, not the window's, should decide the layout. If WKWebView sizes to the visible window instead, desktop.png comes out phone-like or cut; then the window must be sized first (macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift) or the shot taken at the window's width.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":197},"end":{"line":224},"content_hash":"b4b942dbc4b0a6935e516a16716f373b03ef689d4da1a78dda44a496c23adbf6"},"summary":"The desktop screenshot's WebView is laid out 1280 wide inside a window that may be narrower","tags":["unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/eval_config.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:00:54.225259Z","id":"ba6407cfb63baec343d0c37ab2b391137f3539eb24eed772948af9c1cc1e98cd","body":{"detail":"checkSpend multiplies the \\$6 build cap (buildCapUsd, lib/agent/plan.dart) by the prompt count. An app granted `sample` by the harness (HttpGrants in tool/eval/build_eval.dart) can also spend through the daemon, at most its daily cap per app (\\$0.50 by default, crates/clax-server/src/routes/sample.rs) on Haiku 5.5; with one sample prompt that is small. `--no-grant` removes it.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":214},"end":{"line":224},"content_hash":"c8ea937d74c66b4a50d056e85e4584b9829d9119237024e2c78db67cb40383d9"},"summary":"The spend guard counts only the agent's build cap, not the published apps' own AI calls","tags":["revisit:more prompts use sample, or the per-app cap rises","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/build_eval.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:05:15.463735Z","id":"609cb95e956a9c1c1c0f701715e2a45fcbc04919fccf379edcc58e487309bef1","body":{"detail":"stop() completes the build as Ending.cap once FeedbackWorker.stopBuild returns (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart:348-360), which only signals the build's cancel and does not wait for the running continue run. BuildEval.build then snapshots log.runs (build_eval.dart:487-489) while that run's RunRecord is still open (timing empty: cost $0, 0 turns, outcome 'unknown'). Its EvalTimings.stop lands on the old EvalLog only if it arrives before the next build() swaps timings.log and inspector.log (build_eval.dart:457-459); a later one closes the next build's open first run with the cancelled run's figures. In practice _write's screenshots (4 s settle per size) usually cover the gap, so RESULTS.md is most at risk on a slow cancel (a long model turn). Cost under-reported for a capped build understates what the run spent against --max-spend.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":509},"end":{"line":518},"content_hash":"69d869d7680dd9d5a0b1e77814d2667b9b3a209d5ddf3f480e6547bc14af957d"},"suggested_fix":"After stopBuild, wait (bounded) for the worker's in-flight run for aid to end, e.g. until log.current?.timing is non-empty or the worker reports no active run for aid, before completing ended.","summary":"A harness stop (run or time cap) ends the build before the cancelled continue run has stopped, so that run's cost and turns can be missing from the capped build's results","tags":["review:E2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/live_build.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:05:22.203474Z","id":"29854f868e2cd60a77f3b190d722b7ade95514f87247cdcab10fbc84a042db86","body":{"detail":"The daemon is started by DaemonSupervisor with IoProcessStarter (Process.start, normal mode), so a terminal Ctrl-C reaches it through the shared process group, but flutter run's 'q' stops the macOS app with a signal Dart does not handle, and the finally at live_build.dart:180-185 never runs. The run's home (<run>/clax-home) is fresh each run, so no later supervisor's _stopStale finds it; the orphan keeps ANTHROPIC_API_KEY in its environment and serves on a loopback port until killed by hand (its PID is in <run>/clax-home/daemon.json and in eval.log's 'daemon up' line).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":107},"end":{"line":185},"content_hash":"088987a289930904bd631fcfa36a9f51e80fbe931f5976ef6dc990e2a47f1a0f"},"suggested_fix":"Watch ProcessSignal.sigterm and sigint in live_build.dart and run the same worker.stop/supervisor.stop before exit; or have run.sh trap EXIT and stop the PID from <run>/clax-home/daemon.json when that process is still clax.","summary":"Quitting flutter run with q (SIGTERM to the app) or a crash of the app leaves the eval's daemon running: the supervisor's stop is only in the finally block","tags":["review:E2","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/prompts.json","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T21:03:50.989443Z","id":"000aa036450922f530bf256602f39d5051f9c5a9f883b0c7fc65465b9eec653f","body":{"detail":"A 'places I've been' prompt (log places with notes and photos, show them on a map, center on where I am) would cover add_kit's map part, the net declaration of tile.openstreetmap.org and the location capability. Adding a sixth prompt raises the default run's worst case to 6 x $6 = $36, over the $30 default --max-spend (apps/clax_app/tool/eval/eval_config.dart line 170) that apps/clax_app/test/eval/eval_harness_test.dart expects, so it needs either a higher default, replacing a prompt, or running it alone with --prompts.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":32},"content_hash":"b71cb95b5378578ae51b145f8f5570fc43cfbace478ac7caa5a7b471035e3df6"},"summary":"No eval prompt exercises the kit's map","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/live_build.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.295792Z","id":"e749dee5d4842bde8cd33d0f92178725fb086f10a06d9ca327570b92cf4e260b","body":{"detail":"Only flutter analyze and the scripted smoke test (apps/clax_app/test/eval/eval_harness_test.dart) cover this file. Unverified until the first keyed run: that `flutter run -d macos -t tool/eval/live_build.dart` (tool/eval/run.sh) passes the parent environment through to the app (flutter_tools desktop_device.dart starts the executable with the parent's environment), that exit() ends `flutter run`, and that the core the bundle embeds (scripts/build-app-clax.sh macos --debug, which run.sh runs first) opens on the run's support directory under target/flutter-app/eval/ from inside the macOS sandbox and serves the shell to the WebViews on the app's scheme. The first run with a key should use one cheap prompt: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=… just app-eval --prompts workouts --model claude-haiku-5-5 --max-spend 6`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":175},"content_hash":"52ada746fb78a0d640ec8aa2625d49c47557d3b9163835beca6095eb1529c68c"},"summary":"The live eval app has never run: no API key on the machine, and building it would share apps/clax_app/build/macos with the integration tests","supersedes":"8a22fe8fcacdab6159022cceee1a56f4613564d28fb8b4ca8568683e1b133600","tags":["unverified","revisit:the first eval run with an API key","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/live_build.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:56:50.535483Z","id":"fc0bed6998b68755066f4967c3919707c48aa356862f932455d997e71b2201b0","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"The live eval runs no daemon process any more: tool/eval/live_build.dart opens the embedded core inside the app's own process (CoreHost), so a quit or a crash of the app ends the core with it.","supersedes":"29854f868e2cd60a77f3b190d722b7ade95514f87247cdcab10fbc84a042db86","tags":["reason:obsolete","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/build_eval.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:13.672303Z","id":"672199a3558ee3be7a16dcb122c51184fac3fec981a38555f21a99e8365a76f7","body":{"detail":"stop() completes the build as Ending.cap once FeedbackWorker.stopBuild returns (apps/clax_app/lib/agent/worker.dart:348-360), which only signals the build's cancel and does not wait for the running continue run. BuildEval.build then snapshots log.runs (build_eval.dart:487-489) while that run's RunRecord is still open (timing empty: cost $0, 0 turns, outcome 'unknown'). Its EvalTimings.stop lands on the old EvalLog only if it arrives before the next build() swaps timings.log and inspector.log (build_eval.dart:457-459); a later one closes the next build's open first run with the cancelled run's figures. In practice _write's screenshots (4 s settle per size) usually cover the gap, so RESULTS.md is most at risk on a slow cancel (a long model turn). Cost under-reported for a capped build understates what the run spent against --max-spend.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":558},"end":{"line":567},"content_hash":"69d869d7680dd9d5a0b1e77814d2667b9b3a209d5ddf3f480e6547bc14af957d"},"suggested_fix":"After stopBuild, wait (bounded) for the worker's in-flight run for aid to end, e.g. until log.current?.timing is non-empty or the worker reports no active run for aid, before completing ended.","summary":"A harness stop (run or time cap) ends the build before the cancelled continue run has stopped, so that run's cost and turns can be missing from the capped build's results","supersedes":"609cb95e956a9c1c1c0f701715e2a45fcbc04919fccf379edcc58e487309bef1","tags":["review:E2","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/tool/eval/live_build.dart","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:13.765356Z","id":"f793d1a8130dc0de4fd9b93f1560419d5991e1f51072f8a3308da58c2ee65884","body":{"detail":"_Host places each inspector's surface at its size with Clip.none; the screenshot is drawn by the page (web/shell/src/app/host.ts `inspection`), so the WebView's frame width, not the window's, should decide the layout. If WKWebView sizes to the visible window instead, desktop.png comes out phone-like or cut; then the window must be sized first (macos/Runner/MainFlutterWindow.swift) or the shot taken at the window's width.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae)'s record.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":233},"content_hash":"b4b942dbc4b0a6935e516a16716f373b03ef689d4da1a78dda44a496c23adbf6"},"summary":"The desktop screenshot's WebView is laid out 1280 wide inside a window that may be narrower","supersedes":"11c42dd2b34d33057e097fba1b1dfa170676deb416f2f89bb3df5ba557f39a23","tags":["unverified","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
